{:edb/db-before-t 1491 :edb/db-after-t 1492 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534804 50 #inst "2026-10-12T15:17:21.778Z" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186057277 1078 #edb/ref 17592186057279 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186059690 1038 #edb/ref 17592186436629 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186060149 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186060149 1071 "$\\,$ Pay the bill, or your power will be shut off.\n\nWhich conditional statement is logically equivalent to the disjunctive statement above?" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186060149 1071 "Pay the bill, or your power will be shut off.\n\nWhich conditional statement is logically equivalent to the disjunctive statement above?" 13194139534804 17592186045417 false] [17592186060149 1074 "Let's denote by $A$ and $B$ the following statements:\n\n- $A:$ Pay the bill.\n\n- $B:$ Your power will be shut off.\n\nThen, our initial statement can be written as $A∨B,$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬A⇒B.\n$$\n\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $¬A:$ You don't pay the bill.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ If you don't pay the bill, then your power will be shut off." 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436630 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436631 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436632 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436633 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1043 #edb/ref 17592186436634 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1045 "Logical Equivalence with Conditional Statements" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1046 #edb/ref 17592186436634 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436622 1048 #edb/ref 175