17592186045417 true] [17592186436628 1078 #edb/ref 17592186436623 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436628 1079 #uuid "0b770ae3-a6bf-565c-b1f8-035f0cda7d32" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436628 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436629 1069 "q-1477" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436629 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436629 1071 "Simplify the statement $¬(P⇒Q).$" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436629 1072 #uuid "a1135e70-c8a0-50ee-ba8b-a60797a22c04" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436629 1074 "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(P⇒Q)≡¬(¬P∨Q).\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n¬(¬P∨Q)≡¬(¬P)∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nFinally, canceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬P)∧¬Q≡P∧¬Q.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $P∧¬Q.$" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436630 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436632 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436630 1062 #uuid "8b066a8e-899d-55a1-8411-df8d5e53b232" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436630 1063 #edb/ref 17592186379167 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436631 1062 #uuid "b746c91b-d837-5aea-9df8-0783cb162ef2" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436631 1063 #edb/ref 17592186401736 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436632 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436631 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436632 1062 #uuid "c7860837-e731-5c21-a8c2-238981203349" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436632 1063 #edb/ref 17592186060149 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436633 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436630 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436633 1062 #uuid "d47622de-c52c-55f3-b089-ee15881a00d2" 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436633 1063 #edb/ref 17592186389677 13194139534804 17592186045417 true] [17592186436634 1058 #edb/ref 17592186436633 13194139534804